<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Mobistar sees 1997 loss in line with 1996.</title>
<headline>Belgian Mobistar sees 1997 loss in line with 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian-French Mobistar NV, Belgium's second GSM mobile phone operator, said on Thursday it expected 1997 results to be in line with 1996, its start up year when it lost 4.19 billion Belgian francs.</p>
<p>&quot;We see in 1997 a loss which will be about the same as in 1996,&quot; Mobistar financial director Wilfried Verstraete told a news conference on 1996 results.</p>
<p>Chairman John Cordier reiterated that according to the company's business plan, Mobistar was not due to break even for four years.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
